---

## 🧪 Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10 · Integration tests (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test (testsmells.org #3)
**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)
**Integration calibration:** Even for integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell — it introduces non-determinism and slows the suite unconditionally.

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← blocks for 3 seconds regardless of actual timing
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout or use an event/semaphore:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with short intervals, fail fast if not ready within budget
    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3-second floor per run; intermittent failures if system is under load.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org #1)
**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101-108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch will never execute in this test — the inserted user is always a basic `User`, so the `PremiumUser` branch is dead code giving false coverage.

**Fix:** Write two explicit tests — one per type:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_BasicUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscountRate()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — the Premium path is never truly exercised.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (testsmells.org #4)
**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113-119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion — passes even if inserts silently fail
}
```

**Fix:** Assert on the outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — this test cannot detect data loss, constraint violations, or silent truncation.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette (extended catalog)
**Location:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35-38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions with no message parameters. A failure in CI reports only the generic assertion text — the developer must open the source to understand which property was wrong.

**Fix:** Add diagnostic messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow diagnosis in CI; developer must trace the exact line to understand failures.

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written Tests)

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single concern, asserts correct outcome |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is self-documenting (3 items added → assert 3); NOT a magic number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Exercises concurrency and asserts a concrete result |

The setup using an in-memory SQLite connection is also well-designed — it avoids Mystery Guest (no external DB dependency) and provides proper test isolation.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Split into two type-specific tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~15 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling helper |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Add message strings to multi-assert methods |

Fixes 1-2 address **false-pass risk** (tests that look green but prove nothing). Fix 3 addresses **flakiness and speed**. Fix 4 is a maintainability improvement.
